# Graph Inspection Notebook

This notebook inspects the graph builders used by the trajectory models. Use it to verify node counts, edge counts, and sample feature values before training depends on graph outputs.

## Synthetic Sparse Keypoint Graph

```python {"interpreter":"/home/splion/Desktop/personal/interpreting-social-navigation/.venv/bin/python"}
from pathlib import Path
import sys

import numpy as np

repo_root = next(path for path in [Path.cwd(), *Path.cwd().parents] if (path / "src/data").exists())
sys.path.insert(0, str(repo_root / "src"))

from st_graph import build_flat_sparse_keypoint_graph

keypoints = np.arange(3 * 3 * 12 * 2, dtype=np.float32).reshape(3, 3, 12, 2)
graph = build_flat_sparse_keypoint_graph(keypoints)

print("variant:", graph.variant)
print("nodes:", graph.nodes.shape)
print("edges:", graph.edge_features.shape)
print("frame 0 present edges:", len(graph.edges_present[0]))
print("frame 1 present edges:", len(graph.edges_present[1]))
```

